User want to create a promotion by selecting the following scope :
- Region -> from Region hiearchy, user should be able to chose from any node of region hierarchy
- Channel -> from channel_m 
- Customer -> from customer hiearchy , user should be able to choose any nodes of the customer hiearchy
- Products _> user can search directly or should be able to filter through category hiearchy or brand hierarchy 

---
The following information is entered by user while creating:

- Start Date & End Date of promotion , through a calendar picker 
- Promo Mechanics (e.g. Save X% )
    - User will enter things like SAve 50%, Save 10% or any numeric % 

on submitting multiple records are created based on combination of product, customer, region, channel, days(start date to end date) in the postgres: TABLE Fact_Promotions 

    promo_id SERIAL PRIMARY KEY -> autogenerated  (each promotion created will have a common number for all promo lines. Each line will add incremetnally. e.g. -> User create a promo and it creates for e.g. 10 records, first id can be 00011, adn then 00012, 00013 and so on. If User create a seconf promo it may again start from 00021 and then 00022,00023 and so on..  )
    product_id INT REFERENCES Product_M(product_id) ->  product_Id in the promo
    customer_id INT REFERENCES Customer_H(customer_id), the customer _Id can be at any node of customer hiearchy, as entered through scope
    region_id INT REFERENCES Region_H(region_id), the region_Id can be any node 
    channel_id INT REFERENCES Channel_M(channel_id),
    time_id INT REFERENCES Time_M(time_id), time_id will store individually all days between teh start date and end date of the promotion

    -- PROMO DETAILS
    discount_pct NUMERIC(5,2), -> this would be the X value
    promo_price_calculated NUMERIC(10,2), the promo price will be base_price_snapshot * (1 - X)

    -- COST SNAPSHOTS (Captured at promo creation time)
    cogs_snapshot NUMERIC(10,2), -> this is fetched for the customer_id and product_id of this line from the duckdb view costs_allcombo_view against costs_allcombo_view.Rollup_Customer_ID and costs_allcombo_view.Product_ID
    logs_snapshot NUMERIC(10,2), -> this is fetched for the customer_id and product_id of this line from the duckdb view costs_allcombo_view against costs_allcombo_view.Rollup_Customer_ID and costs_allcombo_view.Product_ID

    base_price_snapshot NUMERIC(10,2), -> this is fetched for the customer_id and product_id of this line from the duckdb view prices_allcombo_view.base_price against prices_allcombo_view.Rollup_Customer_ID and prices_allcombo_view.Product_ID
    base_volume_snapshot NUMERIC(10,2), -> this is fetched for the customer_id and product_id of this line from the duckdb view basevolume_allcombo_view.volume against basevolume_allcombo_view.Rollup_Customer_ID and basevolume_allcombo_view.Product_ID
    promo_volume_estimate NUMERIC(10,2), -> this is blank to start with, provide ability to put a value by the user
    incremental_volume NUMERIC(10,2), -> calculated as promo_volume_estimate - base_volume_snapshot
    incremental_revenue NUMERIC(10,2), -> calculated as ((promo_volume_estimate*promo_price_calculated) -            (base_volume_snapshot*base_price_snapshot))

    incremental_margin NUMERIC(10,2), -> calculated as Margin at Promo  - Margin at Base.  Margin at Promo is calculated as promo_volume_estimate * (promo_price_calculated - (cogs_snapshot + logs_snapshot)). margin at base is calculated as base_volume_snapshot * (base_price_snapshot - (cogs_snapshot + logs_snapshot))
